        "question_text": "<p>In a hydraulic brake system, what principle explains the transmission of force from the brake pedal to the brake calipers?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The hydraulic brake system operates based on <b>Pascal's Law</b>, which states that pressure applied to a confined fluid is transmitted undiminished in all directions. This allows a small force at the brake pedal to be multiplied and transmitted to the brake calipers.</p>",
